 "pdf": "ads127l21.pdf",
 "pages": "p.3 (pins), p.5-6 (ROC), p.14-15 (timing), p.36-42 (data rates), p.65-67 (reset, control modes), p.70-75 (SPI, commands, data), p.80-96 (registers)",
 "notModeled": [
  "analog input, buffers, reference, VCM, input range, offset/gain calibration registers (stored only)",
  "programmable FIR / IIR filter coefficient upload (FIR_BANK / IIR_BANK are plain registers here, no coefficient memory) and the coefficient / main memory CRC checks (CRC_ERR, STATUS2 flags never set)",
  "16-bit resolution (CONFIG1.DATA = 1), the optional STATUS1 header byte (CONFIG3.STATUS) and SPI CRC byte: the output frame is always the 24-bit data; SPI_ERR never set",
  "SDO/DRDY DATA_MODE = 10b (data-ready shown also while CS is high) is modeled as 01b",
  "3-wire SPI (CS tied low, CS_MODE) and the SPI reset input pattern; daisy-chain pass-through",
  "synchronized control mode (START_MODE = 10b) converts continuously regardless of START: the model only starts on the START pin / START bit; start/stop mode stops immediately rather than after the ongoing conversion",
  "a register write above CONTROL (05h-17h) restarting the conversion; conversion-start DELAY and the filter latency of the first conversion (Tables 7-4, 7-5, 7-7, 7-9, 7-12): conversion time is the steady 1 / data rate = OSR / fMOD for SPEED_MODE (fCLK 3.2 / 12.8 / 25.6 / 32.768 MHz, fMOD = fCLK / 2) and FLTR_OSR (mid-speed OSR values from Table 8-12); FLTR_SEL, FIR2/FIR3/IIR stage settings do not change it",
